<Post slug="commercial-cleaning-cost-naples-fl" faqs={faqs}>
  <p>If you run a business in Naples, Bonita Springs, Estero or Marco Island, one of the first questions you have about commercial cleaning is simple: what will it cost? The honest answer is that it depends on your space. But "it depends" is not very useful, so this guide explains exactly what it depends on, how we calculate an estimate, and what typical monthly ranges look like.</p>

  <h2>The four things that drive the price</h2>
  <h3>1. Size</h3>
  <p>Square footage is the starting point. A bigger space takes longer to clean, so the price grows with the size. But it does not grow perfectly in a straight line: very small spaces still need travel and setup, which is why every visit has a minimum.</p>
  <h3>2. Type of space</h3>
  <p>A square foot of open warehouse is very different from a square foot of medical exam room. Spaces with more restrooms, more touch points and more people take more time per foot. In our estimator, medical and dental offices and gyms have the highest rate per square foot, standard offices and retail sit in the middle, and open warehouse space has the lowest.</p>
  <h3>3. Frequency</h3>
  <p>How often we clean changes both the price per visit and the monthly total. When we clean often, each visit is a bit faster because the space never gets very dirty, so the price per visit goes down. But you pay for more visits, so the monthly total goes up. A space cleaned once a month needs more work per visit than one cleaned three times a week.</p>
  <h3>4. Your specific needs</h3>
  <p>Extra tasks, like a large kitchen, many glass partitions, special floors or a required disinfectant, can change the price. That is why the final price always comes from a walkthrough.</p>

  <h2>How our estimate is calculated</h2>
  <p>Our online estimator uses a simple, transparent formula:</p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Price per visit</strong> = square feet × rate for your type of space × frequency adjustment. If the result is below our minimum per visit, the minimum applies.</li>
    <li><strong>Monthly cost</strong> = price per visit × average visits per month (for example, 3 visits a week is about 13 visits a month).</li>
    <li><strong>Range</strong> = the monthly cost, plus and minus 15%, rounded to the nearest $10.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>The range is wide on purpose. Two offices with the same square footage can need very different amounts of work, and we would rather give you an honest range than a precise-looking number that changes after we see the space.</p>

  <h2>Example monthly ranges</h2>
  <p>Here are approximate ranges from our estimator at the time of writing. They are examples, not quotes, and our rates can change. Use the <a href="/estimate">estimator</a> for a range based on today's rates and your own space.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Office, 3,000 sq ft, cleaned 3 times a week:</strong> about $1,130 to $1,520 per month.</li>
    <li><strong>Medical office, 2,000 sq ft, 3 times a week:</strong> about $1,220 to $1,650 per month. Smaller than the office, but more work per square foot.</li>
    <li><strong>Retail store, 1,500 sq ft, once a week:</strong> about $310 to $420 per month. At this size the minimum per visit applies.</li>
    <li><strong>Warehouse, 20,000 sq ft, twice a week:</strong> about $2,710 to $3,670 per month. A large space, but open floor costs much less per foot.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>For spaces over 25,000 square feet, the estimator still shows a range, but we recommend a free walkthrough before you rely on it.</p>

  <h2>What is usually included</h2>
  <p>A regular commercial cleaning visit usually covers trash and recycling, dusting and wiping surfaces, disinfecting touch points, cleaning restrooms and kitchens, restocking supplies you provide, and vacuuming and mopping floors. Each of our <a href="/services/office-cleaning">service pages</a> lists what is included for that type of space.</p>
  <p>Things like carpet extraction, floor stripping and waxing, outside windows or post-construction cleanup are usually quoted separately.</p>

  <h2>How to keep the cost down</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Match frequency to traffic.</strong> A quiet office may not need daily cleaning. A busy one probably needs more than once a week. Our guide on <a href="/blog/how-often-should-a-business-be-cleaned">how often a business should be cleaned</a> can help.</li>
    <li><strong>Focus on the rooms that matter.</strong> Restrooms, kitchens and entries need the most attention. Low-use storage rooms may only need a visit every so often.</li>
    <li><strong>Keep clutter off surfaces.</strong> Clear desks and counters are faster to clean well.</li>
    <li><strong>Adjust by season.</strong> In Southwest Florida, many businesses are busier in winter. You can add visits in the busy months and scale back in summer.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Getting an exact price</h2>
  <p>The fastest way to know your real price is a free walkthrough. We visit your space in <a href="/locations/naples">Naples</a>, <a href="/locations/bonita-springs">Bonita Springs</a>, <a href="/locations/estero">Estero</a> or <a href="/locations/marco-island">Marco Island</a>, look at every room, ask how your business runs, and send a written monthly quote with the tasks, days and times. Start with the <a href="/estimate">online estimate</a> to see where you are likely to land.</p>
